          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of the
            %em PL de Rham complex
            (
            %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"}> Bousfield-Gugenheim 76
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Sullivan77"} Sullivan 77
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            which applies to general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %p
            The terminology “PL” for “piecewise linear” seems to have been tacitly introduced in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BousfieldGugenheim76"} Bousfield-Gugenheim 76
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#GriffithMorgan13"} Griffith-Morgan 13
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+differential+forms"} polynomial
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
          %p
            In analogy to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+theorem"} de Rham theorem
            for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dg-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dg-algebraic rational homotopy theory
            shows that the PL de Rham complex computes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+cohomology"} rational cohomology
            (or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+cohomology"} real cohomology
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+cohomology"} complex cohomology
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
          %p
            Applied to a topological space that happens to carry the structure of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zig-zag"} zig-zag
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
            to the smooth
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            in the
